.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-step 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-step \- Answer a step from its receipt when its exact inputs, arguments and tools already passed
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten step\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Answer a step from its receipt when its exact inputs, arguments and tools already passed
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
batten\-step\-check(1)
Say hit or miss for a step\*(Aqs inputs, arguments and tools, and remember the key a record must match
.TP
batten\-step\-record(1)
Record that a step passed, refusing when its inputs changed since the paired check
.TP
batten\-step\-run(1)
Run a step\*(Aqs command only when its receipt misses, and record the receipt when it passes
.TP
batten\-step\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
